# R8 keep rules. AGP combines every file in src/main/keepRules and passes the
# result to R8.
#
# Almost nothing here is needed for ordinary Kotlin code: R8 follows normal
# call graphs perfectly well, and Room, Compose and Navigation all ship their
# own rules inside their artifacts. What R8 cannot see is code reached from
# outside the JVM — which, in this app, means the speech recogniser.

# --- Vosk / JNA -------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Vosk is a native library driven through JNA. JNA maps Java classes onto C
# structs and functions by *name*, at runtime, via reflection: rename or remove
# one and the mapping fails with an UnsatisfiedLinkError that only appears in a
# minified build. Nothing in the bytecode tells R8 these are used, so they are
# kept wholesale.
-keep class org.vosk.** { *; }
-keep class com.sun.jna.** { *; }
-keep class * implements com.sun.jna.Library { *; }
-keep class * extends com.sun.jna.Structure { *; }
-keep class * extends com.sun.jna.PointerType { *; }

# JNA looks these up reflectively on the classes above.
-keepclassmembers class * extends com.sun.jna.Structure {
    public <fields>;
}

# JNA references optional platform classes that are not present on Android.
-dontwarn java.awt.**
-dontwarn com.sun.jna.**

# --- Room -------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Room generates its implementations at build time and ships consumer rules for
# them, so nothing is needed here. The entities are kept because their column
# names are matched by field name in the generated cursor readers.
-keepclassmembers class code.opensource0000.justnotes.data.local.** {
    <fields>;
}
